Cross-reference — DIS-01 Rev 4 §3.6 (Controlled-capacity recognition)	
A limit below nameplate is recognized only with a valid UL 1741 / UL 3141 PCS certification plus an approved Control Narrative — sufficient in themselves for recognition. Where the site's arrangement includes utility equipment, the recognized limit is enforced as applicable: telemetry monitoring, and on pure-generation sites the POI recloser's ANSI 32 directional-power element set to the recognized limit and tripping on violation.	
How to use this list	
The Inverters tab lists smart-inverter models with a valid UL 1741-SB certification of record as of the edition date. The Power Control Systems tab lists UL 3141-certified PCS assemblies eligible to satisfy the controlled-capacity recognition path under DIS-01 §3.6. Listing on this edition does not by itself authorize interconnection; project-specific screening, protection, and commissioning requirements continue to apply. Models superseded, delisted, or withdrawn between quarterly editions are removed from the current tab; superseded editions remain available through Standards Engineering on request.	
Change summary since CEL-2024-Q4	
— 8 inverter models added on new UL 1741-SB certifications received 11/2024–04/2025.	
— 2 inverter models removed — manufacturer discontinued line or certification not renewed under UL 1741-SB.	
— 3 PCS models added (Quenda Controls QC-PCS-250; Verronex Power Systems VPS-Cap-1500; Verronex Power Systems VPS-Cap-3000).	
— All Torvane Electric TE-75K rows recertified to UL 1741-SB; superseded UL 1741 (non-SB) entry retired.	
